  "question": {
    "text": "If $z=x$ - iy and $z^{1 / 3}=p+$ iq $(x, y, p, q \\in \\mathbb{R})$, then $\\frac{\\left(\\frac{x}{p}+\\frac{y}{q}\\right)}{\\left(p^2+q^2\\right)}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "I4jhf",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IfBrY",
      "text": "-1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ttVAq",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fmXlj",
      "text": "$-2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$z=p^3-3 p q^2+i\\left(3 p^2 q-q^3\\right)=x-i y$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n&x=p\\left(p^2-3 q^2\\right) \\\\\n&y=-q\\left(3 p^2-q^2\\right) \\\\\n&\\therefore \\frac{x}{p}+\\frac{y}{q}=p^2-3 q^2-3 p^2+q^2=-2\\left(p^2+q^2\\right)\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
